<!-- | Feature/Gaps           | Status    | Technical Observation                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |
| **Peripheral Type**    | **Decoder**| Hardware Motion JPEG Decoder (JDEC). Used for frame decompression in the Multimedia (D0) domain.                                                                                                                                                                                       |
| **Control Registers**  | **FULL**  | `jdec_control_1` (0x00) controls core features like YUV format, swap mode, U/V order, and burst lengths (XLEN). `jdec_control_3` (0x1C) handles interrupt enable/status and operational flags (idle, func).                                                                           |
| **Frame Buffers**      | **FULL**  | `jdec_yy_frame_addr` (0x08) and `jdec_uv_frame_addr` (0x0C) define the start addresses for Y (luminance) and UV (chrominance) output buffers.                                                                                                                                           |
| **Address Pointers**   | **FULL**  | Registers `jp_addr0` through `jp_addr_f` (0x40-0x7C) form a crucial 16-entry table of pointers, likely used by the hardware for linked-list JPEG stream processing or multi-frame decoding. These are read-only status registers based on the header.                                      |
| **Frame Dimensions**   | **FULL**  | `jdec_frame_size` (0x2C) defines the image resolution in MCU blocks (WBLK/HBLK). `jdec_header_skip` (0x30) allows skipping header bytes if the JPEG stream is partially pre-processed.                                                                                                   |
| **Interrupts/Status**  | **FULL**  | Explicit W1P (`reg_int_clr`, `reg_yuv_frame_pop`) for clearing status. `jp_frame_cnt` provides the count of JPEG frames ready for processing.                                                                                                                                            |
| **Base Address**       | Explicit | 0x30023000 (MJDEC_BASE in `bl808.h`).                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |
-->
